umos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/87/388087/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0d62bc2a647f07ab0f6b3b76cd74a92fb8c853bf" commit="0126000ec97e2601ad84d93cb1e72e39267290c4" commit_message="config_lib: Save only meaningful template values.  Templates often have values like the default build config. Since build configs are rebuilt from json with default + template + config, there is no need to save anything from a template that is different from default.  Also, templates can contain callables, or delete_key values which can't be correctly serialized to json. This CL resolves them to concrete values before saving.  I further tested by comparing cbuildbot_view_config --full from before/after. Nothing changed other than the template dumps, which proves this didn't break anything.  BUG=chromium:645296 TEST=run_tests  Change-Id: I0d62bc2a647f07ab0f6b3b76cd74a92fb8c853bf Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/389251 Commit-Ready: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="389251" owner_email="dgarrett@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/51/389251/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iec612340113baf81c01da702d1c774fc390c6a83" commit="5d0dbbd5ee2890d359460ba044ee3f2611c6380c" commit_message="Add --gn-args parameter to deploy_chrome for future use by the chromeos-chrome ebuild.  This also outputs GYP_DEFINES and GN_ARGS taken from the environment as info logging for debuging builders.  BUG=chromium:636622 TEST=./cbuildbot/run_tests scripts/deploy_chrome_unittest  Change-Id: Iec612340113baf81c01da702d1c774fc390c6a83 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388900 Commit-Ready: Steven Bennetts &lt;stevenjb@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Steven Bennetts &lt;stevenjb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="388900" owner_email="stevenjb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/00/388900/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3bc6c3390c6bc631ff78b5747c374a788dfdac60" commit="e2e214b6acf2de4386a7456b1540652a09394266" commit_message="Upload a tarball containing only debug/breakpad.  The new tarball debug_breakpad.tar.xz contains only files in debug/breakpad, which can be used to symbolicate dumps collected during test.  BUG=chromium:623739 TEST=unittest(cbuildbot/run_tests), trybot  Change-Id: I3bc6c3390c6bc631ff78b5747c374a788dfdac60 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388798 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="388798" owner_email="dshi@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/98/388798/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1d0070f54beb4088c892b36cfabcfaec1ec322ac" commit="8b8c42e92e2ff2b8097d51d7b24e1cb7ebd77108" commit_message="add missing local markings &amp; quotes  Some of these functions corrupt variables because they don't declare them as local (so they break the parent).  Add missing local markings and a few quotes while I'm here.  BUG=chromium:644845 TEST=precq passes TEST=installing from USB stick still works  Change-Id: I1d0070f54beb4088c892b36cfabcfaec1ec322ac Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/387346 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="387346" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/crosutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crosutils" ref="refs/changes/46/387346/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibdface9f7a76186e210ef0f4111cd5fe9905bba9" commit="c1ba008667b052cc0f692fef2ffac89e7be8b352" commit_message="cr50: tpm: ignore sys_rst_l/plt_rst_l when TPM reset is in progress  There is no point in invoking TPM reset while the current invocation is in progress. One of the cases when this is happening is early start up on Kevin/Gru: the device starts booting, the EC comes around to pulsing sys_rst_l when TPM is already busy installing endorsement certificates.  There is no point in issuing another reset at that point, just let the process continue.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:52366 TEST=firmware_TPMKernelVersion firmware_TPMExtend autotests still pass      on kevin. Certificate installation during startup does not get      interrupted any more.  Change-Id: Ibdface9f7a76186e210ef0f4111cd5fe9905bba9 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/389811 Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="389811" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/11/389811/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie7e0ddfa3328a1d57565ce72f46e72ad58db2f10" commit="291566c5697172f56bf415671a388d09b221f9c8" commit_messag